  "id": "Compound::DB00786 - Gene::4317",
  "verbalization": "Marimastat is likely to interact with Matrix Metalloproteinases (MMPs) through binding to specific MMPs such as Mmp23b, Mmp27, or Mmp26, which are all members of the MMP family. These MMPs are involved in the regulation of extracellular matrix remodeling, a process critical in various physiological and pathological contexts. The shared participation of these MMPs in the same pathway suggests a common functional role, potentially linking Marimastat to the broader MMP-mediated signaling network. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust, biologically relevant interaction, though the exact molecular mechanism of binding remains to be elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights Marimastat's potential role in modulating MMP activity, which could have implications for therapeutic applications targeting extracellular matrix dynamics.",
